onential Growth Expression Using Percentage Growth" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110626 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186110332 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110626 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "dcd3e634-d64c-57dc-9d4c-8f7f67c731ab" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110858 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186111536 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110858 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186111537 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110858 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186111538 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110858 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110858 #edb/ref 1045 "Creating Exponential Growth Expressions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110858 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186111536 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110858 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050886 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110858 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "f15731b1-3f94-5cda-9865-241f1ae29ba5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111207 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186108967 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111207 #edb/ref 1069 "q-45632" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111207 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111207 #edb/ref 1071 "At the beginning of a study, a beehive had $4\\,000$ bees. The study showed that the number of bees in the hive doubles every week. How many bees will be in the hive after $3$ weeks?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111207 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e84b8561-bf3c-52d8-8533-88bb8eb9ad86" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111207 #edb/ref 1074 "The hive starts with $4,000$ and then doubles every week. \n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n- After $1$ week, there are $4\\,000\\cdot 2$ bees.\n\n- After $2$ weeks, there are $4\\,000\\cdot {2}^{2}$ bees.\n\n- After $3$ weeks, there are $4\\,000\\cdot {2}^{3}$ bees.\n\nSo the correct expression for the number of bees after $3$ weeks is $4\\,000\\cdot {2}^{3}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111536 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111537 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111536 #edb/ref 1061 193608 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111536 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "868a0a9f-3d0c-5548-b4c4-a2688c08805c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111536 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186111914 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111537 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111538 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111537 #edb/ref 1061 193609 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111537 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "cc23439c-f454-5e68-a5a0-22cdf9bf2e0f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111537 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186110625 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111538 #edb/ref 1061 193613 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111538 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8da3c630-d870-51f5-bf19-afa5e49a3cbb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111538 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186110626 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111914 #edb/ref 1064 "A biologist is experimenting with bacteria stored in a Petri dish. She observes that the number of bacteria in the dish *triples* every hour. If there were $100$ bacteria initially, can she determine how many bacteria will be present after $3$ hours?\n\nStarting with $100$ bacteria, she knows that this number *triples* after one hour. Remember that tripling means to multiply by a factor of $3$.\n\nTo get the number of bacteria after one hour, we multiply the initial amount by $3$:\n\n$$\n\\color{blue}{100\\cdot 3}\n$$\n\nAfter another hour ($2$ hours in total), the number above triples again. So to get the total number of bacteria after $2$ hours, we multiply the amount above by $3$:\n\n$$\n({\\color{blue}{100\\cdot 3}})\\cdot 3 = {\\color{red}{100 \\cdot 3^2}}\n$$\n\nAnd after another hour ($3$ hours total), the number above triples once again:\n\n$$\n({\\color{red}{100 \\cdot 3^2}})\\cdot 3 = 100 \\cdot 3^3\n$$\n\nIf we evaluate the above expression, we get\n\n$$\n100 \\cdot 3^3 = 100\\cdot 27 = 2\\,700\n$$\n\nSo after $3$ hours, there will be $2\\,700$ bacteria in the Petri dish.\n\nThis is an example of **exponential growth**. The number of bacteria triples over a time interval of $1$ hour, every hour. The total number of bacteria grows very rapidly, as we can see from the chart below.\n\n![](images/bf/bf039743a936cab0ca74708584fc3670202588d15fc63a4257ad1a737047da2d.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111914 #edb/ref 1065 8841 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111914 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "60dc9833-8054-5a01-9e29-d592d2e4498a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111914 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490505 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186491258 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490505 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186491268 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490505 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186491270 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490505 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490505 #edb/ref 1045 "Creating Exponential Growth Expressions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490505 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186491258 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490505 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046648 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490505 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050886 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490505 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "9e157ec6-4793-57c2-b506-87c05869c40b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490553 #edb/ref 1080 "101\\,000" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490553 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490553 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "14b09e89-02e2-512e-b84a-5ca59c815d96" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490585 #edb/ref 1080 "81\\,000" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490585 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490585 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2873b67c-4668-555a-9f4a-0e815ba69aeb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490593 #edb/ref 1080 "2\\cdot (1.02)^{4}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490593 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490593 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2a5b533e-8c41-5f4b-88da-6d0580536264" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186490597 #edb/ref 1080 "79\