186555825 #edb/ref 1071 "One month, a greengrocer sold $40$ kilograms of watermelon. If the number of kilograms of sold watermelon doubles each month, how many kilograms of watermelon will the greengrocer sell after $4$ months?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555825 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7c172a4f-97f6-5647-a1db-039307497883" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555825 #edb/ref 1074 "In a particular month, the greengrocer sold $40$ kilograms of watermelon, and then this amount doubles every month.\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n- After $1$ month, the greengrocer will sell $40\\cdot 2$ kilograms of watermelon.\n\n- After $2$ months, the greengrocer will sell $40\\cdot {2}^{2}$ kilograms of watermelon.\n\n- After $3$ months, the greengrocer will sell $40\\cdot {2}^{3}$ kilograms of watermelon.\n\n- After $4$ months, the greengrocer will sell $40\\cdot {2}^{4}$ kilograms of watermelon.\n\nSo the correct expression is $40\\cdot {2}^{4}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555868 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186555641 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555868 #edb/ref 1069 "q-61650" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555868 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555868 #edb/ref 1071 "Rose's initial salary was $$10\\,000$, and her salary increased by $12%$ per year. To the nearest $$10$, what was Rose's salary $3$ years later?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555868 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ebeb4e55-43ec-53a6-b8e8-b7cfc99f6520" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555868 #edb/ref 1074 "Rose received $$10\\,000$ initially, and this amount increased by $12%$ each year.\n\n$12%$ as a decimal is $0.12.$ Therefore, an increase of $12%$ corresponds to multiplication by a factor of\n\n$$\n1+0.12=1.12.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n- After $1$ year, Rose received $10\\,000\\cdot (1.12)$ dollars.\n\n- After $2$ years, Rose received $10\\,000\\cdot (1.12)^{2}$ dollars.\n\n- After $3$ years, Rose received $10\\,000\\cdot (1.12)^{3}$ dollars.\n\nEvaluating the expression for the amount of money received after $3$ years, we get\n\n$$\n10\\,000\\cdot (1.12)^{3}≈14\\,050.\n$$\n\nAfter $3$ years, Rose received approximately $14\\,050$ dollars." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555920 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "84d2439c-12b2-5f43-8e1a-04cf836fad55" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555920 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186555825 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555937 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186555940 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555937 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "cd3ae942-426d-56b9-afd0-f43d65368750" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555937 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186111207 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555940 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186555920 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555940 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "cfda6eef-02c1-5673-89c5-c06fdbcb6a52" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186555940 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186555868 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
